{"rec":"tier","name":"unit","what":"no real time, no sockets, no network, no outside services or toolchains beyond the Go test binary; stays inside its working directory"}
{"rec":"tier","name":"functional","what":"uses a real thing: a compiler or VM, a toolchain, generated code built and run; per pull request on runners that provide it"}
{"rec":"tier","name":"nightly","what":"heavy or long: long fuzz, full matrices, soak, timing, anything past a two-minute job even sharded"}
{"rec":"type","name":"roundtrip","what":"read bytes, write them back, same bytes"}
{"rec":"type","name":"encode","what":"a value written from scratch gives exactly the expected bytes"}
{"rec":"type","name":"decode","what":"bytes read give exactly the expected value"}
{"rec":"type","name":"write-refusal","what":"writing a bad value is refused (debug assert in the assert legs; every build in the refuse legs)"}
{"rec":"type","name":"load-refusal","what":"hostile bytes are refused in every build, with the named reason"}
{"rec":"type","name":"codegen","what":"generated source compiles and is clean"}
{"rec":"type","name":"golden","what":"the generated source or output for a schema and language equals its pinned file"}
{"rec":"type","name":"name-check","what":"a schema's names are accepted or refused by the name checker"}
{"rec":"type","name":"evolution","what":"one schema version reads or writes another's data"}
{"rec":"type","name":"fuzz","what":"seeded mutations"}
{"rec":"type","name":"plant","what":"a negative control: a named test run against a deliberately broken build must come out red"}
{"rec":"type","name":"compiler","what":"the compiler or IR itself (parse, check, plan), with no generated language involved"}
{"rec":"type","name":"tooling","what":"CI policy, docs, roadmap, repo-structure and harness self-tests"}
{"rec":"type","name":"bench","what":"performance or timing"}
{"rec":"type","name":"lint","what":"generated or runtime code is clean under the language's strict analyser"}
{"rec":"type","name":"differential","what":"two implementations or two versions give the same answer"}
{"rec":"type","name":"soak","what":"long-running repeated use, with no leak or drift"}
{"rec":"type","name":"resource-bounds","what":"memory, allocation and depth limits are held"}
{"rec":"type","name":"model","what":"a TLA+ model checks under TLC, or a code trace is a behaviour of the spec"}
{"rec":"group","name":"pr","what":"the pull-request tier: unit and functional tests of every language whose adapter has landed, and every language-free test","query":{"ready":true,"tiers":["unit","functional"]}}
{"rec":"group","name":"nightly","what":"everything, every language: a language with no adapter is red here, and its red count is its remaining work","query":{"tiers":["unit","functional","nightly"]}}
